<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01HE">Remark <span data-tag="01HE">4.5.5.13</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a pushout diagram of simplicial sets </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ A \ar [r]^-{f} \ar [d]^{g} &amp;  A_0 \ar [d]^{g'} \\ A_1 \ar [r] &amp;  A_{01}, } \]
</div>
<p> where $f$ is a monomorphism. If $g$ is a categorical equivalence, then $g'$ is also a categorical equivalence. This follows by combining Example <a data-tag="01FJ" href="/tag/01FJ">4.5.5.12</a> with Proposition <a data-tag="01FC" href="/tag/01FC">4.5.5.10</a>. </p>
